In order to prevent duplicate user entries with the same circle_id and
address from showing up in the database, createUser should recover
soft-deleted users instead of creating a new entry with the same address
alongside the soft-deleted entry.

This is relevant for the coordinape user in #558

test plan:
1. create a user in an existing circle:
    ```gql
    mutation MyMutation {
      createUser(payload: {
        address: "0x02675dfa4d4d6b3fb7d04e0c8ad000eff752bd89", 
        circle_id: 1, 
        name: "dopeocount"
      }) {
        id
        UserResponse {
          address
        }
      }
   }
   ```
2. soft-delete the user:
    ```sql
    UPDATE users
    SET deleted_at = 'now()'
    WHERE name = 'dopeocount'
    ;
    ```
3. recreate the user:
   ```gql
    mutation MyMutation {
      createUser(payload: {
        address: "0x02675dfa4d4d6b3fb7d04e0c8ad000eff752bd89", 
        circle_id: 1, 
        name: "dopeocount"
    }) {
        id
        UserResponse {
          address
        }
      }
    }
   ```
4. Verify that the same row in the database is returned and no duplicate
   rows exist.

